- `ERC721.transferFrom(from,to,ticketId)` is the direct inherited external transfer route. It rejects zero `to`, calls this override with `_msgSender()` as nonzero authorization input, and then requires the returned previous owner to equal caller-supplied `from` (`target/packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:L114-L125`; dynamic override at `target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L497-L502`). Thus destination/factory reads occur before the inherited authorization check, while the `from` equality check occurs after the update and reverts the transaction if it fails (`target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L498-L501`; `target/packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:L119-L124`, `L216-L242`).
